#
# The homomorphicEncryption flagship's worked example: the exact output of the native producer
# math::producers::additive_he_demo (dogfooded — the worked example IS what the producer emits;
# the explicit `stage-math-producers` boundary asserts this fixture is graph-isomorphic to the
# producer's Turtle, so neither can silently drift). A math:HomomorphicEncryptionScheme
# declaring the operation it is math:homomorphicOver, its math:securityAssumption
# (math:learningWithErrors), its math:noiseModel, and — as a math:RingHomomorphism — its
# math:preservedOperation and its math:preservationLaw. The scheme's additive-homomorphic law
# Dec(Enc(a) ⊕ Enc(b)) = a ⊕ b is verified exactly in the producer. Conforms to
# math:HomomorphicEncryptionSchemeShape, math:HomomorphismShape, and math:PreservationLawShape.
# Bound by ex:ecHeSchemeProduced.
@prefix math:  <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix mprod:     <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/math/producers/> .

# Flagship 2 — an exact additive-homomorphic encryption scheme.
# Dec(Enc(a) ⊕ Enc(b)) = a ⊕ b holds exactly over ℤ_q; verified in-code.
mprod:heScheme a math:HomomorphicEncryptionScheme ;
    math:homomorphicOver mprod:heAdd ;
    math:preservedOperation mprod:heAdd ;
    math:preservationLaw mprod:heLaw ;
    math:securityAssumption math:learningWithErrors ;
    math:noiseModel mprod:heNoise .

mprod:heAdd a math:Operation .
mprod:heLaw a math:Axiom .
mprod:heNoise a math:MathematicalObject .
